{
  "analysis": "The previous command showed the contents of panel.tsv, samples.tsv, controls.tsv, acquisition_notes.md, and gating_sop.md. Key observations:\n1. 6 PBMC samples: D617, D685, D735, D829 (voltage group 1, YG780-A at 641 V), and D858, D960 (voltage group 2, YG780-A at 703 V).\n2. Controls include single stains. Note that PerCP-Cy5.5 bead control has lot 2807268, but ctrl_PerCPCy55_cells.fcs has lot 3066970 (which matches panel.tsv lot 3066970).\n3. YG780-A (PE-Cy7) was rerun at the higher voltage: ctrl_PECy7_rerun.fcs and fmo_HLADR_rerun.fcs.\n4. Need to determine how spillover matrix is constructed for each sample.\n5. Need to check gating SOP and compensation acceptance check.",
  "plan": "Write a python inspection script to examine the FCS headers, spillover keywords in files, detector names, voltages, and explore the single-stain controls.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 -c \"\nimport os, flowkit as fk\nprint('Flowkit version:', fk.__version__)\n\"\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat << 'EOF' > inspect_session.py
import glob, os
import fcsparser

files = sorted(glob.glob('/task/input/fcs/*.fcs'))
